@* _MentionRenderer — M36 (ADR 0165 D6) the @mention render pass at the
   MarkdownRenderer boundary. Renders the content's Markdown body through the
   FROZEN MarkdownRenderer (unchanged, M36·6 — the one-renderer pin), then
   runs the M36 mention pass (Kumunita.Web.Security.MentionRenderer) to
   linkify each resolved @<DisplayName> into <a class="mention"
   href="/directory/{id}">@<DisplayName></a>. Emits via Html.Raw (the body is
   already escape-first-rendered by the MarkdownRenderer; the pass only wraps
   a resolved token in an anchor whose href is a platform-relative
   /directory/{id} — a "link is not a grant," D5: the directory gate runs on
   click).

   Shape note (drift, U07): the register's U07 deliverable + design-doc Part
   2.4 prose name a client-side mention-renderer.ts IIFE, but Part 2.7's
   MentionRendererTests is a C# xunit class and Part 2.8's acceptance gate is
   C# (dotnet exec) — a C# test cannot execute a TS IIFE. ADR 0165 D6
   Consequences permit "a server-side pass in the MarkdownRenderer boundary,"
   and the C# MentionRendererTests + the MarkdownRenderer (C#, Security/)
   precedent make the server-side C# pass the only shape that satisfies the
   milestone's gate. This partial is that wire-in (one of the two named
   shapes, not a third). See the MentionRenderer class doc for the full note.

   Graceful floor: the two frozen seams (IMentionService + DirectoryService)
   are resolved from the request services; if either is absent (a minimal
   test harness) the pass is skipped and the plain Markdown body renders —
   a safe no-op (no mention links, no error). In production both are DI-
   registered (U03 / M2), so the pass always runs there. *@
@using Kumunita.Web.Security
@using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection
@model Kumunita.Web.Views.Shared.MentionBodyModel
@{
    string final;
    var sp = ViewContext.HttpContext.RequestServices;
    var mentions = sp.GetService<Kumunita.Core.Mentions.IMentionService>();
    var directory = sp.GetService<Kumunita.Core.UserInfo.DirectoryService>();
    if (mentions is not null && directory is not null)
    {
        // The content's author's subject id (the self-exclusion input, M36-5 /
        // ADR 0165 D2): the author is never mentioned by their own name. This
        // is the <b>same</b> input the emitter's resolver used (the content
        // author, not the viewer), so a name that resolved for emission resolves
        // for the link — and the author's own name is inert in both. (The
        // caller passes AuthorSubjectId; a guest's view of another's content
        // still excludes that content's author from mentions.)
        string authorId = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.AuthorId)
            ? string.Empty
            : Model.AuthorId;
        var map = await MentionRenderer.BuildMapAsync(mentions, directory, Model.Body, authorId);
        final = MentionRenderer.Render(MarkdownRenderer.RenderHtml(Model.Body), map);
    }
    else
    {
        // Floor: no mention pass (seams absent) — render the plain Markdown
        // body. A safe no-op; no mention links, no error.
        final = MarkdownRenderer.RenderHtml(Model.Body);
    }
}
@Html.Raw(final)
